= Artificial intelligence — Technical =

== Problem formulations ==
AI systems are commonly modeled through one or more of:

<pre>
state / observation
action
transition dynamics
objective / utility / reward
knowledge or belief state
inference / search / planning procedure
learning procedure
</pre>

Different subfields emphasize different parts of this structure.

== Symbolic and statistical approaches ==
Symbolic AI represents states, rules, relations, goals, or knowledge explicitly.

Statistical and machine-learning approaches learn predictive or decision structure from data.

Modern systems often combine learned models with explicit search, retrieval, planning, constraints, tools, or symbolic interfaces.

== Scope ==
No single capability test defines the entire field.

AI includes narrow task systems, general-purpose models, agents, robots, planning systems, and multi-agent systems.

